+$|1-e^{i\theta}|=\varepsilon$ and $0<|\theta|\le\pi$; then
+$\varepsilon=2\sin(|\theta|/2)\le|\theta|$.  Let
+$n=\lceil\pi/(3|\theta|)\rceil$, the least integer with
+$n|\theta|\ge\pi/3$.  If $n=1$ then $n|\theta|=|\theta|\le\pi$;
+otherwise $|\theta|<\pi/3$ and minimality gives
+$n|\theta|<\pi/3+|\theta|<2\pi/3$.  In both cases
+$\pi/3\le n|\theta|\le\pi$, so
+$|1-e^{in\theta}|=2\sin(n|\theta|/2)\ge2\sin(\pi/6)=1$.  Since
